.AVIATION...
(18Z TAFS)
Issued at 1156 AM PDT Mon Aug 31 2026

Finishing Fogust off strong with a robust marine layer at a depth of
around 2200 feet this morning. MVFR stratus will take a bit longer
to scatter out today, likely in the early afternoon. Moderate
onshore winds increase through the day and ease slightly overnight.
APC and LVK may experience gusts up to 20 kt through the late
afternoon which will gradually diminish tonight. Medium confidence
on how widespread the marine layer will be tonight as an upper level
trough approaches our coast. This trough may generate sufficient
lifting to mix out the marine layer across the North Bay, but
confidence remains low. Higher confidence for coastal sites to
develop MVFR ceilings around sunset with HAF likely to stay cloudy
all day.

Vicinity of SFO...MVFR stratus persists into the afternoon as
moderate westerly winds increase. There has been some disagreement
in the model guidance on whether stratus will completely scatter out
today. Currently on satellite, there is some dry air making its way
to our coast. This dry air combined with a moderate onshore flow
may be enough to scatter out the remaining clouds in the SF Bay.
MVFR ceilings return as winds ease to gentle and persist into
Tuesday afternoon. Medium confidence on the overall forecast.

SFO Bridge Approach...Stratus is likely to become patchy over the
bridge before scattering out at the terminals this
morning/early afternoon. Otherwise, similar to SFO.

Monterey Bay Terminals...Northwest to westerly breezes increase to
moderate this afternoon as MVFR ceilings scatter out. The marine
layer is less likely to mix out due to the upper level trough,
therefore anticipate an early return of MVFR ceilings right
around sunset.

